Good catch - the regression from 2f7420ccaacb ("riscv: mpfs: move SoC level
options to the CPU Kconfig") did indeed swap "imply MICROCHIP_COREQSPI" for
"imply MICROCHIP_QSPI", and MICROCHIP_QSPI isn't a defined Kconfig symbol in
drivers/spi, so the imply was silently a no-op rather than failing the build.

One-line fix, matches the symbol actually defined by the in-tree CoreQSPI
driver and the MPFS DT nodes, as you note. This is a trivial, obviously
correct fix - fine by inspection. Has anyone actually confirmed build/boot
on MPFS hardware with CoreQSPI enabled after this change (as opposed to just
confirming the Kconfig symbol now resolves)?
